    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Torque from tension",
      "description": "Only the component of tension perpendicular to the beam contributes to torque. This component is T sin θ. It acts at a distance L, producing a counterclockwise torque of magnitude τ_tension = (T sin θ) × L."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Rotational equilibrium",
      "description": "For the beam to remain horizontal, the net torque about the hinge must be zero. Set the magnitudes equal: T sin θ × L = Mg × (L/2)."
